WEBVTT

00:00:19.660 --> 00:00:21.300
(Lee Je Hoon)

00:00:21.370 --> 00:00:23.270
(Jang Hyuk Jin, Bae Yoo Ram, Kim Eui Sung, Pyo Ye Jin)

00:00:34.910 --> 00:00:37.420
(Taxi Driver 3)

00:00:37.480 --> 00:00:38.480
(This drama is a work of fiction.)

00:00:38.480 --> 00:00:39.480
(All people, incidents, and backgrounds...)

00:00:39.550 --> 00:00:41.150
(in this drama are fictitious.)

00:00:41.220 --> 00:00:42.220
(Children and animals were filmed under guidelines.)

00:00:43.290 --> 00:00:44.290
One. (Support Admin Watch on
kissasia.cam or kisskh.org)

00:00:44.720 --> 00:00:47.160
- Two. Three. - Two. Three.

00:00:47.590 --> 00:00:48.590
- Four. - Four.

00:00:49.090 --> 00:00:52.000
One, two, three, four.

00:00:52.060 --> 00:00:54.470
- Move it! One. - One.

00:00:54.870 --> 00:00:55.870
One.

00:00:56.330 --> 00:00:59.200
One, two, three, four.

00:01:00.840 --> 00:01:02.640
- Hey. - Comsec.

00:01:03.040 --> 00:01:04.840
The training's pretty brutal, right?

00:01:06.380 --> 00:01:07.380
Tell me about it.

00:01:07.880 --> 00:01:10.980
Rookies are supposed to get stuck with the tough training, you know?

00:01:12.180 --> 00:01:14.450
Speaking of which, I have a drill the day after tomorrow.

00:01:15.220 --> 00:01:16.990
Seriously? It wasn't on the schedule.

00:01:17.060 --> 00:01:20.260
Yes. It's a joint operation with the artillery unit.

00:01:20.330 --> 00:01:22.490
A combat tactical drill for a B24 point-of-origin strike.

00:01:22.960 --> 00:01:26.000
A combat tactical drill? I guess we can't talk for a while.

00:01:26.100 --> 00:01:27.170
Yes, looks like it.

00:01:27.570 --> 00:01:30.600
When you get your training bonus, you owe me barbecue and drinks.

00:01:31.270 --> 00:01:32.640
Nice try. You're buying.

00:01:33.540 --> 00:01:34.740
Talk to you when you get back.

00:01:35.710 --> 00:01:38.440
Roger that. Good luck out there.

00:01:38.680 --> 00:01:39.680
Okay.

00:01:43.750 --> 00:01:45.320
According to an intelligence report,

00:01:45.820 --> 00:01:49.520
the risk of a localized provocation by North Korea's army is increasing.

00:01:50.190 --> 00:01:52.560
The objective of this drill...

00:01:52.920 --> 00:01:55.660
is to ensure we are fully prepared for a surprise North Korean attack.

00:01:56.790 --> 00:02:00.100
Assume the North will attack with their most elite forces.

00:02:02.600 --> 00:02:05.370
Effective immediately, per this drill's security protocol,

00:02:05.640 --> 00:02:07.040
all personnel will surrender their cell phones...

00:02:07.840 --> 00:02:09.940
and conduct an inspection of all personal firearms and gear.

00:02:11.110 --> 00:02:12.680
Master Sergeant Yoo, stay. The rest of you, dismissed!

00:02:13.140 --> 00:02:14.710
On your feet!

00:02:16.510 --> 00:02:18.449
Salute the Commander!

00:02:18.450 --> 00:02:19.950
- Unity! - Unity!

00:02:21.520 --> 00:02:22.550
Unity!

00:02:25.590 --> 00:02:26.590
Dismissed!

00:02:28.030 --> 00:02:29.960
- As you were! - As you were!

00:02:39.340 --> 00:02:40.340
Here.

00:02:41.740 --> 00:02:46.180
- What is this, sir? - Tomorrow, your team skips K43.

00:02:47.380 --> 00:02:48.980
You'll move to Sector B24 instead.

00:02:50.280 --> 00:02:51.780
Sector B24, sir?

00:02:52.420 --> 00:02:56.820
I've marked the coordinates. Report to me as soon as you arrive.

00:02:58.020 --> 00:02:59.020
Any questions?

00:03:03.190 --> 00:03:04.200
No, sir.

00:03:04.760 --> 00:03:06.160
Unity.

00:03:06.800 --> 00:03:07.770
Dismissed.

00:03:20.480 --> 00:03:22.350
Tomorrow, your team skips K43.

00:03:23.180 --> 00:03:24.880
You'll move to Sector B24 instead.

00:03:25.220 --> 00:03:27.320
A combat tactical drill for a B24 point-of-origin strike.

00:04:04.820 --> 00:04:05.820
Unity!

00:04:06.160 --> 00:04:08.329
- Sir, I'll drive! - Just get in. We're out of time.

00:04:08.330 --> 00:04:09.330
Yes, sir.

00:05:08.320 --> 00:05:11.390
You'll move to Sector B24 instead.

00:05:12.520 --> 00:05:13.520
B24.

00:05:16.090 --> 00:05:17.460
They're going here at this hour?

00:05:51.860 --> 00:05:54.300
(Sector B24)

00:06:08.150 --> 00:06:11.150
It's all getting torched anyway. Did you have to bring so much?

00:06:11.380 --> 00:06:13.520
I prepared everything as instructed by General Oh.

00:06:13.890 --> 00:06:15.020
General Oh, I swear.

00:06:15.790 --> 00:06:17.789
The MDL explosion?

00:06:17.790 --> 00:06:19.760
- Good prep. - Thank you, sir.

00:06:22.160 --> 00:06:24.060
- What was that? - Sir? What is it?

00:06:24.730 --> 00:06:25.730
Didn't you hear that?

00:06:26.160 --> 00:06:27.300
I didn't hear a thing, sir.

00:06:28.800 --> 00:06:30.640
Never mind. Let's unload the vests first.

00:06:30.900 --> 00:06:31.900
Yes, sir.

00:07:00.530 --> 00:07:01.530
Five.

00:07:02.230 --> 00:07:03.230
Six.

00:07:04.570 --> 00:07:05.570
Seven.

00:07:06.770 --> 00:07:08.010
You really can't tell the difference.

00:07:08.170 --> 00:07:10.340
Be careful, sir! It could go off!

00:07:11.210 --> 00:07:13.380
It even weighs about the same as the standard vest.

00:07:13.910 --> 00:07:16.080
But sir, isn't blowing up all eight of them a bit much?

00:07:16.850 --> 00:07:19.050
You arrogant jerk. You must've lost your mind.

00:07:19.180 --> 00:07:21.250
I'm sorry, sir. I'll drive!

00:07:24.860 --> 00:07:26.120
Blow them up?

00:08:01.030 --> 00:08:05.200
(C4 military-grade explosive)

00:08:18.340 --> 00:08:19.640
Unit, attention!

00:08:21.110 --> 00:08:22.980
Salute the commander!

00:08:23.350 --> 00:08:24.680
Unity!

00:08:26.750 --> 00:08:27.820
Unity!

00:08:32.820 --> 00:08:33.820
At ease!

00:08:34.730 --> 00:08:36.090
About-face!

00:08:38.200 --> 00:08:39.360
Commence training!

00:08:39.660 --> 00:08:40.670
- Commence! - Commence!

00:08:54.510 --> 00:08:57.580
This live drill prepares us for North Korean provocations.

00:08:57.720 --> 00:09:00.349
You will all advance as far as the northern perimeter of the GOP.

00:09:00.350 --> 00:09:02.050
Upon arrival at Sector B24,

00:09:02.320 --> 00:09:06.160
equip vests from the barracks and move out immediately.

00:09:06.660 --> 00:09:08.930
But sir, isn't blowing up all eight of them a bit much?

00:09:11.030 --> 00:09:14.370
This is a critical mission, so give it your absolute all,

00:09:14.570 --> 00:09:17.170
and get the best rating. Understood?

00:09:17.340 --> 00:09:18.470
- Yes, sir! - Yes, sir!

00:09:26.140 --> 00:09:27.980
Get in the passenger seat. I'm driving.

00:09:29.580 --> 00:09:31.780
- Move it! - Yes, ma'am.

00:10:08.090 --> 00:10:09.090
Get out.

00:10:09.620 --> 00:10:11.560
- I said, get out! - Yes, ma'am!'

00:10:14.090 --> 00:10:15.590
Everyone, dismount the truck.

00:10:16.730 --> 00:10:17.730
Move it! Out!

00:10:18.330 --> 00:10:19.330
- Yes, ma'am! - Yes, ma'am!

00:10:24.940 --> 00:10:28.270
Effective immediately, you will all return to base.

00:10:29.340 --> 00:10:31.540
- We must have misheard you, ma'am. - You heard me, didn't you?

00:10:31.910 --> 00:10:33.080
Everyone, return to base!

00:10:33.580 --> 00:10:34.680
- Yes, ma'am! Understood! - Yes, ma'am! Understood!

00:11:26.000 --> 00:11:28.100
This is Training Headquarters. Team Alpha, do you copy?

00:11:29.600 --> 00:11:30.600
Team Alpha?

00:11:32.540 --> 00:11:34.710
Team Alpha, acknowledge transmission immediately!

00:11:35.870 --> 00:11:39.780
I repeat. This is Training HQ. Team Alpha, do you copy?

00:11:41.250 --> 00:11:44.180
- Team Alpha, answer me! - Let me.

00:11:44.750 --> 00:11:45.920
This is the Commander.

00:11:46.780 --> 00:11:48.190
Master Sergeant Yoo, what is your location?

00:11:50.790 --> 00:11:52.960
I know what you were planning to do to us.

00:11:53.260 --> 00:11:54.260
What?

00:11:54.730 --> 00:11:57.600
What did you possibly hope to gain by sending your men to their deaths?

00:11:58.230 --> 00:12:00.000
Master Sergeant Yoo Sun A, what are you talking about...

00:12:00.060 --> 00:12:02.230
What were you planning to do with those bomb vests?

00:12:03.330 --> 00:12:05.440
She's lost her darn mind.

00:12:05.800 --> 00:12:07.810
If you can't answer me, then I'm going...

00:12:08.270 --> 00:12:11.180
straight to the Military Prosecution with what you've planted here.

00:12:11.380 --> 00:12:15.680
Hey, Yoo Sun A! You know this is insubordination!

00:12:47.210 --> 00:12:49.980
(Ministry of National Defense Initial report: Explosion near MDL)

00:13:09.870 --> 00:13:10.870
Let's do this.

00:13:35.260 --> 00:13:36.430
Master Sergeant Yoo Sun A!

00:13:37.090 --> 00:13:39.100
Are you really disobeying a direct order?

00:13:39.760 --> 00:13:40.800
Are you?

00:13:43.630 --> 00:13:45.370
You're no longer soldiers.

00:13:45.840 --> 00:13:47.200
Get ready to be dishonorably discharged.

00:13:47.710 --> 00:13:50.140
You're not getting out of here with that stuff anyway.

00:13:51.180 --> 00:13:53.340
Yoo Sun A, think this through.

00:13:54.240 --> 00:13:56.680
I don't know what on earth has gotten into you,

00:13:57.150 --> 00:13:59.020
but you're almost up for your pension.

00:13:59.280 --> 00:14:00.920
If you get discharged for pulling a stunt like this,

00:14:01.590 --> 00:14:03.790
how is your mother supposed to get by?

00:14:05.860 --> 00:14:07.589
Let's say we've acquired critical intelligence,

00:14:07.590 --> 00:14:10.590
but on our way back to base, we run into an unavoidable problem.

00:14:11.060 --> 00:14:12.730
What do we do with the intel?

00:14:12.960 --> 00:14:14.730
Your safety comes before the intel.

00:14:15.230 --> 00:14:16.870
If your safety isn't guaranteed,

00:14:17.470 --> 00:14:18.940
you abandon the critical intelligence.

00:14:22.770 --> 00:14:24.140
If you stop right now,

00:14:25.280 --> 00:14:26.640
I'll make this all go away.

00:14:27.850 --> 00:14:31.320
Master Sergeant Yoo, let's just drop this. All right?

00:14:32.050 --> 00:14:33.250
Cut the nonsense.

00:14:39.590 --> 00:14:41.690
That road only leads to North Korea.

00:14:42.290 --> 00:14:43.760
What are you going to do, defect to the North with it?

00:14:44.500 --> 00:14:45.600
This is your last chance.

00:14:46.400 --> 00:14:48.070
If you don't surrender right now,

00:14:48.530 --> 00:14:51.740
Master Sergeant Yoo Sun A, you'll be seen as an armed deserter.

00:14:52.070 --> 00:14:56.810
(Military Demarcation Line)

00:14:57.980 --> 00:14:58.980
Darn it!

00:15:33.080 --> 00:15:34.080
But if, despite all that,

00:15:34.580 --> 00:15:36.880
you find yourself in a life-or-death situation,

00:15:37.510 --> 00:15:40.850
you pass on the intel using our team's protocol.

00:16:04.170 --> 00:16:06.440
What is that protocol?

00:16:06.580 --> 00:16:07.580
(Landmine)

00:16:07.710 --> 00:16:12.250
Find the bird's nest in the closest tree due west...

00:16:12.780 --> 00:16:14.050
and secure the intel inside it.

00:16:43.980 --> 00:16:46.050
If anything should happen to me,

00:16:49.220 --> 00:16:50.890
I'm trusting you to find this.

00:16:51.620 --> 00:16:52.720
Captain Kim Do Gi.

00:17:29.390 --> 00:17:31.160
That crazy wench.

00:18:16.540 --> 00:18:18.740
That darn commie jerk just won't listen.

00:18:19.640 --> 00:18:20.980
What should we report to the command?

00:18:23.350 --> 00:18:24.380
Weren't you listening?

00:18:25.920 --> 00:18:28.320
That commie jerk smuggled out weapons...

00:18:28.620 --> 00:18:30.090
to try and sell them to the North,

00:18:30.850 --> 00:18:32.090
and ended up getting killed in an accident.

00:18:32.520 --> 00:18:35.260
Yes, sir. I'll write up the incident report just like that.

00:18:35.630 --> 00:18:36.830
Darn it.

00:18:37.190 --> 00:18:39.760
The general will ream me out for this.

00:18:46.600 --> 00:18:49.840
Master Sergeant Yoo Sun A gave up her life...

00:18:50.370 --> 00:18:51.680
to save her comrades.

00:18:53.080 --> 00:18:54.080
Exactly.

00:18:57.750 --> 00:18:59.080
And that's what makes this even more infuriating.

00:18:59.950 --> 00:19:02.690
And nobody even knows she was murdered so unjustly.

00:19:03.050 --> 00:19:04.660
The jerks who did this to Master Sergeant Yoo Sun A...

00:19:05.860 --> 00:19:07.220
are still out there, walking free.

00:19:09.630 --> 00:19:10.760
But we know the truth.

00:19:13.830 --> 00:19:14.970
So we have to fight.

00:19:19.270 --> 00:19:20.600
It's going to be a tough fight.

00:19:21.770 --> 00:19:24.680
And it won't be over quickly. You know that too, Captain.

00:19:32.380 --> 00:19:34.020
But if you're doing this, Captain,

00:19:34.650 --> 00:19:35.890
I'll see it through with you.

00:19:38.620 --> 00:19:40.460
The methods you're used to, Master Sergeant Park,

00:19:41.220 --> 00:19:42.530
won't work on these people.

00:19:43.890 --> 00:19:44.900
Sir?

00:19:46.600 --> 00:19:49.200
For people who defy all common sense,

00:19:50.930 --> 00:19:53.240
we have to be unreasonable right back.

00:19:54.710 --> 00:19:56.010
It's the only way.

00:20:05.780 --> 00:20:12.819
(Taxi Driver 3)

00:20:12.820 --> 00:20:16.590
(Taxi Driver 3)

00:20:21.870 --> 00:20:23.300
Are these the people you called?

00:20:23.930 --> 00:20:25.670
Yes, they are.

00:20:26.200 --> 00:20:27.770
They are ecological survey specialists.

00:20:28.610 --> 00:20:29.910
Then why did you lie about being a general?

00:20:30.310 --> 00:20:32.679
What? I never said such a thing.

00:20:32.680 --> 00:20:34.040
Hey, you said he pulled rank.

00:20:34.780 --> 00:20:37.310
When we asked who he was, he just said he was a general.

00:20:37.550 --> 00:20:40.480
He said if we didn't open the gate, he'd just turn around and leave.

00:20:40.550 --> 00:20:42.989
I didn't say I was a general.

00:20:42.990 --> 00:20:44.520
I said, "I'm Jang Seong Cheol."

00:20:45.120 --> 00:20:47.359
My name is Jang Seong Cheol.

00:20:47.360 --> 00:20:49.630
Besides, if you won't open, what can I do? I should turn around.

00:20:49.930 --> 00:20:51.600
I ran a check on you too. Nothing came up.

00:20:53.300 --> 00:20:54.400
I'm not surprised you couldn't find me.

00:20:55.270 --> 00:20:56.270
You see, I am...

00:20:56.970 --> 00:21:00.270
a ghost agent. I exist, but on paper, I don't.

00:21:01.370 --> 00:21:02.910
But you said he's your son.

00:21:04.470 --> 00:21:05.840
This is technically classified.

00:21:06.910 --> 00:21:09.550
I'm his team leader. He's like a son to me.

00:21:09.610 --> 00:21:10.710
And he's like a father to me.

00:21:13.680 --> 00:21:14.680
Why that...

00:21:15.490 --> 00:21:16.490
Then what's this?

00:21:17.020 --> 00:21:18.290
We didn't want to show up empty-handed.

00:21:19.520 --> 00:21:21.960
So, you're all here to research birds?

00:21:22.730 --> 00:21:24.630
- Yes. - And your affiliation?

00:21:24.800 --> 00:21:25.800
That's classified.

00:21:27.800 --> 00:21:30.100
You took the motor pool logs, didn't you?

00:21:30.500 --> 00:21:33.000
- Yes. - For your darn bird investigation?

00:21:35.440 --> 00:21:37.270
- That's classified. - Hey!

00:21:38.140 --> 00:21:40.780
Birds are pretty free-spirited, aren't they?

00:21:43.450 --> 00:21:45.220
Are these guys messing with me?

00:21:54.320 --> 00:21:56.860
- Hello? - Colonel Kim Tae Hyun.

00:21:57.230 --> 00:21:59.260
This is Major General Jo Sang Hoon from Special Ops.

00:21:59.630 --> 00:22:02.200
- Sir, Unity! - Right. Keep up the hard work.

00:22:02.930 --> 00:22:05.300
Did the people I sent make it there okay?

00:22:08.210 --> 00:22:10.570
The Black Eagle Team. You're the one who sent them, sir?

00:22:11.740 --> 00:22:15.210
It's of national importance, so make sure you look after them.

00:22:15.850 --> 00:22:18.780
Help them with anything they need. All right, carry on.

00:22:35.900 --> 00:22:38.100
I know what you were planning to do to us.

00:22:39.370 --> 00:22:42.210
What did you possibly hope to gain by sending your men to their deaths?

00:22:42.940 --> 00:22:44.570
Master Sergeant Yoo Sun A, what are you talking about...

00:22:44.640 --> 00:22:46.740
What were you planning to do with those bomb vests?

00:22:49.150 --> 00:22:51.110
If you can't answer me, then I'm going...

00:22:51.880 --> 00:22:54.850
straight to the Military Prosecution with what you've planted here.

00:23:05.830 --> 00:23:09.430
What kind of person could even think about killing their own soldiers?

00:23:10.100 --> 00:23:12.740
That Master Sergeant Yoo Sun A was really something else.

00:23:13.040 --> 00:23:14.040
So courageous.

00:23:18.480 --> 00:23:20.880
You should've told us this was happening.

00:23:21.580 --> 00:23:23.050
Why did you just leave without a word?

00:23:24.310 --> 00:23:26.620
You even ditched your phone and were completely unreachable.

00:23:26.880 --> 00:23:28.590
You knew we'd be worried sick.

00:23:29.190 --> 00:23:30.190
I'm sorry.

00:23:30.520 --> 00:23:33.390
It was too personal. I couldn't ask you guys for help.

00:23:33.990 --> 00:23:36.430
That's even more reason to ask for our help.

00:23:36.730 --> 00:23:38.130
Hang on a second.

00:23:38.500 --> 00:23:41.530
Driver Kim called us for a personal matter?

00:23:41.830 --> 00:23:42.930
He even sent us a page.

00:23:43.630 --> 00:23:46.740
This is basically a job request from Driver Kim. Right?

00:23:47.440 --> 00:23:49.909
- It's totally a job request. - Exactly.

00:23:49.910 --> 00:23:51.170
- A job request? - I even had to...

00:23:51.470 --> 00:23:52.980
return to the military.

00:23:53.340 --> 00:23:55.110
How much is the taxi fare going to be for this?

00:23:55.450 --> 00:23:58.580
Captain, so you're saying these people came here in a taxi?

00:23:59.580 --> 00:24:02.249
All right, it looks like everyone's caught up.

00:24:02.250 --> 00:24:04.350
I think we have some work to do here.

00:24:05.060 --> 00:24:06.660
What's our first move?

00:24:10.360 --> 00:24:11.360
We need to find them.

00:24:12.030 --> 00:24:15.000
Who did this, and why.

00:24:15.730 --> 00:24:17.269
We've found two so far.

00:24:17.270 --> 00:24:18.670
The colonel and the first lieutenant.

00:24:18.800 --> 00:24:21.470
You need higher command approval to form a temporary unit...

00:24:21.670 --> 00:24:22.970
and plan a joint operation.

00:24:23.040 --> 00:24:25.180
You're saying a general is involved.

00:24:26.340 --> 00:24:28.080
Someone who would go as far as killing their own allies...

00:24:28.980 --> 00:24:30.510
just for personal gain.

00:24:31.510 --> 00:24:33.280
Do you have anyone in mind?

00:24:34.320 --> 00:24:35.820
One person comes to mind,

00:24:36.450 --> 00:24:38.050
but he's in no position to be doing something like this right now.

00:24:38.290 --> 00:24:40.590
- Either way, I'm in. - Me too.

00:24:41.590 --> 00:24:44.130
Just don't make us worry like that again.

00:24:45.900 --> 00:24:47.360
I'm docking the taxi fare from your paycheck.

00:24:49.230 --> 00:24:52.600
I'm sorry, Captain. I have no idea what this is about.

00:24:56.640 --> 00:25:01.010
I'm on board too. What a great plan.

00:25:08.920 --> 00:25:10.749
Radio Operator!

00:25:10.750 --> 00:25:12.090
The power's out! Go check it!

00:25:12.560 --> 00:25:14.520
You can't just flip random breakers like that.

00:25:14.590 --> 00:25:17.189
Look, I know it's a hassle. That's why I brought this order.

00:25:17.190 --> 00:25:18.430
Look there.

00:25:18.560 --> 00:25:20.500
See the wire? There's a bird's nest on the wire.

00:25:20.560 --> 00:25:22.730
If you leave that on, what happens to us?

00:25:22.800 --> 00:25:24.129
That's not it. If we cut the power now,

00:25:24.130 --> 00:25:26.600
our security will be compromised! This is wrong, I'm telling you.

00:25:27.540 --> 00:25:29.210
Just a little more! A little more.

00:25:29.370 --> 00:25:30.910
Just stall for time.

00:25:31.140 --> 00:25:32.940
If you turn it on now, I'll die!

00:25:33.210 --> 00:25:35.780
- He'll die! - Hey, Radio Operator.

00:25:35.850 --> 00:25:37.950
It's still not working. Hurry and check it.

00:25:38.010 --> 00:25:39.820
I'm just checking on the nest right now.

00:25:39.980 --> 00:25:42.320
- Tell him he'll be dead instantly! - We might as well just die.

00:25:42.390 --> 00:25:44.219
We're out of time. Should we die?

00:25:44.220 --> 00:25:46.020
Bury me at the National Cemetery!

00:25:46.120 --> 00:25:48.430
- I... - Do you want to end up in the brig?

00:25:48.490 --> 00:25:51.160
- How much longer? - All right. Five seconds!

00:25:51.230 --> 00:25:53.500
- Five seconds! - Five seconds. Not six, five.

00:25:53.560 --> 00:25:56.170
- Hey, Radio Operator. - Yes, I'm checking it right now.

00:25:56.230 --> 00:25:57.929
- Aren't you done yet? - Three seconds.

00:25:57.930 --> 00:26:00.040
- Three seconds. - Three seconds.

00:26:00.300 --> 00:26:03.610
- Okay. Transfer complete. - Okay. We're done here too.

00:26:04.810 --> 00:26:06.310
We did it!

00:26:08.480 --> 00:26:10.980
The PC is booting up. It's coming up.

00:26:11.350 --> 00:26:13.350
Hey, the comms are back up. You did great.

00:26:14.150 --> 00:26:15.690
I've secured all the data we need.

00:26:16.990 --> 00:26:18.220
Man, that was tough.

00:26:20.690 --> 00:26:23.430
You've got what it takes to be a true soldier.

00:26:25.560 --> 00:26:28.830
- Let's go. - A true soldier! One, two, three.

00:26:29.670 --> 00:26:32.540
Captain, who did you call? What do they do?

00:26:32.900 --> 00:26:36.010
I still have absolutely no idea what you're trying to accomplish.

00:26:36.310 --> 00:26:38.980
Sometimes in life, things happen that defy common sense,

00:26:39.480 --> 00:26:42.210
and you must be the one to respond. Remember I said that?

00:26:42.980 --> 00:26:43.980
Yes.

00:26:45.650 --> 00:26:47.219
Whatever you see, Master Sergeant Park,

00:26:47.220 --> 00:26:48.450
I need you to look the other way.

00:26:49.250 --> 00:26:50.290
And trust me.

00:26:51.890 --> 00:26:54.590
If that's an order, sir, I'll do it.

00:26:57.030 --> 00:26:59.330
Then again, I didn't understand what you were saying anyway.

00:27:02.900 --> 00:27:08.040
(Citizen happiness, national prosperity)

00:27:55.350 --> 00:27:58.790
(Lunar calendar, October 10)

00:28:02.960 --> 00:28:03.960
It is done!

00:28:17.640 --> 00:28:18.840
November?

00:28:19.980 --> 00:28:21.380
There's not much time left.

00:28:27.450 --> 00:28:29.390
(Colonel Kim Tae Hyun)

00:28:29.450 --> 00:28:31.350
(Command center)

00:28:33.990 --> 00:28:35.660
The person you are trying to reach is unavailable...

00:28:54.440 --> 00:28:56.350
(Bird investigation)

00:29:00.120 --> 00:29:03.120
This is the 2802nd Unit's roster for the next operation.

00:29:03.190 --> 00:29:04.490
(Unit 2802, Additional deployment roster)

00:29:04.550 --> 00:29:07.320
Hey, this is classified information. How did you get this?

00:29:07.520 --> 00:29:09.429
They're restarting the operation that failed...

00:29:09.430 --> 00:29:10.860
because of Master Sergeant Yoo.

00:29:12.400 --> 00:29:13.600
Under the guise of a training exercise.

00:29:15.000 --> 00:29:17.630
Shouldn't we stop this exercise immediately, Driver Kim?

00:29:17.800 --> 00:29:19.470
What do we do now, Driver Kim?

00:29:21.240 --> 00:29:23.070
Driver Kim?

00:29:24.370 --> 00:29:27.239
- Why is everyone calling you that? - Master Sergeant Park.

00:29:27.240 --> 00:29:29.149
Yes, Driver Kim Do Gi. No, I mean, Driver.

00:29:29.150 --> 00:29:30.710
No, Captain. Yes.

00:29:31.280 --> 00:29:33.020
Master Sergeant Park, you will return to your original unit today.

00:29:33.220 --> 00:29:35.080
But sir, I'd like to stay and help.

00:29:35.350 --> 00:29:36.620
I have a job for you back at your unit.

00:29:37.020 --> 00:29:38.150
Can I ask you for a favor?

00:29:38.520 --> 00:29:40.790
Of course. If it's for you, I'll do anything you ask.

00:29:41.990 --> 00:29:44.860
- Go Eun, I have a favor to ask you. - Yes? What is it?

00:29:55.370 --> 00:29:57.770
(Command center)

00:29:57.840 --> 00:29:59.110
I'm sorry to keep calling you.

00:29:59.910 --> 00:30:02.550
I wonder what has our Tae Hyun in such a hurry?

00:30:03.150 --> 00:30:04.650
A new investigation team has arrived at the base,

00:30:05.180 --> 00:30:06.820
and more than a few things about them are suspicious.

00:30:07.420 --> 00:30:11.320
Above all, this guy, Kim Do Gi, was the late Yoo Sun A's commander.

00:30:12.020 --> 00:30:15.690
With something this big planned, we can't afford any suspicion.

00:30:17.190 --> 00:30:19.160
Weeds must be pulled out from the root.

00:30:21.330 --> 00:30:23.330
(Establishing military discipline)

00:30:23.370 --> 00:30:24.770
Hello, is this the Human Rights Center?

00:30:25.540 --> 00:30:27.840
I have something to report. I'm heading over right now.

00:31:05.840 --> 00:31:06.840
Hello?

00:31:08.950 --> 00:31:10.210
Is anybody here?

00:31:52.720 --> 00:31:53.720
(Special Warfare School)

00:32:03.300 --> 00:32:05.570
Go Eun. Go Eun, are you okay?

00:32:06.440 --> 00:32:07.440
I'm okay.

00:32:47.610 --> 00:32:50.180
(Lieutenant General Oh Won Sang)

00:32:51.910 --> 00:32:52.920
Come in.

00:32:56.690 --> 00:32:57.690
Unity!

00:32:59.920 --> 00:33:02.020
I have selected the elite personnel you requested.

00:33:04.130 --> 00:33:05.600
You're more proactive than I expected.

00:33:08.400 --> 00:33:10.930
And your training evaluations are always top-notch.

00:33:12.030 --> 00:33:14.140
- You've earned your reputation. - Thank you, sir.

00:33:14.970 --> 00:33:19.380
But I haven't been briefed yet. What is the mission, sir?

00:33:20.640 --> 00:33:22.610
I have a special mission in mind,

00:33:23.510 --> 00:33:25.210
and I'm thinking of entrusting it to you.

00:33:26.520 --> 00:33:28.180
Pull this off, and I'll make sure you get promoted.

00:33:35.790 --> 00:33:39.230
Intel confirms an inspection tour near Kaesong on December 13.

00:33:41.660 --> 00:33:44.100
(Predicted Route and Operation Plan)

00:33:44.370 --> 00:33:47.370
Take a platoon under your command, send them in,

00:33:47.970 --> 00:33:49.370
and take his head this time.

00:33:51.070 --> 00:33:52.640
I don't see an extraction route, sir.

00:33:53.780 --> 00:33:54.780
Extraction?

00:33:55.610 --> 00:33:58.210
According to this plan, they'll run out of fuel infiltrating.

00:33:59.150 --> 00:34:01.450
- Extraction will be impossible. - Right.

00:34:01.880 --> 00:34:03.020
You don't have to go.

00:34:04.050 --> 00:34:06.420
Send your best soldiers. Don't worry about the rest.

00:34:07.790 --> 00:34:12.330
Without an extraction route, the entire team will be killed, sir.

00:34:13.500 --> 00:34:15.200
For this kind of mission, the fewer people know, the better.

00:34:21.770 --> 00:34:22.770
Captain Kim Do Gi.

00:34:24.610 --> 00:34:25.710
You know about pigs, right?

00:34:27.280 --> 00:34:29.450
You fatten them up just for a single slaughter.

00:34:30.710 --> 00:34:33.150
Those men you're training... They're all pigs.

00:34:35.280 --> 00:34:38.220
You use them for one thing only. Only once.

00:34:39.990 --> 00:34:41.420
Do you understand what I'm saying?

00:34:46.560 --> 00:34:47.560
Is this...

00:34:49.970 --> 00:34:50.970
an order, sir?

00:34:55.240 --> 00:34:57.640
I'm not in a position to ask favors, am I?

00:35:04.380 --> 00:35:05.880
Crystal clear, sir.

00:35:06.780 --> 00:35:07.920
I'll begin preparations at once, sir.

00:35:09.420 --> 00:35:10.450
Unity!

00:35:12.660 --> 00:35:14.120
Good. That's how you get ahead.

00:35:15.490 --> 00:35:16.490
Unity.

00:35:30.910 --> 00:35:33.980
(Indomitable Spirit, Absolute Loyalty and Obedience)

00:35:34.110 --> 00:35:35.950
(Special Warfare Command)

00:35:41.950 --> 00:35:44.090
All personnel are on standby for deployment, sir.

00:35:44.490 --> 00:35:46.590
- About today's operation... - Yoo Sun A.

00:35:47.290 --> 00:35:48.290
Park Jae Won.

00:35:48.291 --> 00:35:49.360
- Yes, sir. - Yes, sir.

00:35:50.290 --> 00:35:53.260
As of today, the entire company is on leave.

00:35:54.030 --> 00:35:55.030
Sir?

00:35:56.230 --> 00:35:57.230
I must have misheard you, sir.

00:35:57.330 --> 00:36:00.600
You did well in the last evaluation, and I still owe you a reward.

00:36:00.840 --> 00:36:02.170
So this is it.

00:36:03.270 --> 00:36:06.740
From this moment on, until you receive another order,

00:36:07.240 --> 00:36:09.850
no one is to return to base. Under any circumstances.

00:36:11.550 --> 00:36:12.580
Understood?

00:36:13.250 --> 00:36:15.020
- Sir? - Yes, sir!

00:36:16.050 --> 00:36:17.120
Yes, sir!

00:36:28.160 --> 00:36:29.770
- Unity. - Unity.

00:36:32.170 --> 00:36:33.170
Unity.

00:36:50.950 --> 00:36:52.760
It was the man I suspected.

00:36:52.990 --> 00:36:55.760
After his dishonorable discharge for sexual harassment,

00:36:55.990 --> 00:36:58.030
our records show he's raising snakes and chickens in the country.

00:36:58.430 --> 00:36:59.430
He's a civilian now.

00:37:00.360 --> 00:37:02.730
A civilian is controlling the military?

00:37:03.170 --> 00:37:04.630
Seriously? How is that even possible?

00:37:05.470 --> 00:37:08.600
The impossible is happening as we speak.

00:37:09.810 --> 00:37:12.270
He knew our every move.

00:37:13.010 --> 00:37:16.580
The men who attacked Driver Kim and me were soldiers.

00:37:16.880 --> 00:37:19.920
That means he already has his hooks in the military.

00:37:21.050 --> 00:37:23.020
This is far more dangerous than we realized.

00:37:56.220 --> 00:37:58.490
My fellow citizens.

00:37:59.760 --> 00:38:04.760
Today, in Sector B24 near the Military Demarcation Line,

00:38:05.900 --> 00:38:10.730
the North Korean Army launched a large-scale armed provocation.

00:38:13.000 --> 00:38:16.470
Our brave soldiers of the Republic of Korea...

00:38:17.440 --> 00:38:21.910
have fallen in an attack by the enemy.

00:38:24.110 --> 00:38:28.480
This massive, deadly attack by North Korea...

00:38:35.360 --> 00:38:40.130
is an assault on our freedom, democracy,

00:38:41.360 --> 00:38:43.500
and the foundation of our constitutional system.

00:38:44.330 --> 00:38:47.500
It is a crime against humanity.

00:38:49.040 --> 00:38:52.210
Our government, in accordance with the Constitution,

00:38:56.010 --> 00:38:58.110
and the procedures established by law,

00:38:58.380 --> 00:39:03.550
to ensure the security of the nation and the safety of its people,

00:39:04.920 --> 00:39:08.020
and under the authority of Article 77 of the Constitution...

00:39:08.890 --> 00:39:11.530
and Article two of the Martial Law Act,

00:39:12.900 --> 00:39:18.130
declares emergency martial law throughout the Republic of Korea.

00:39:21.070 --> 00:39:24.110
I hear you were promoted to general. Congratulations.

00:39:24.370 --> 00:39:26.340
It's all thanks to your support.

00:39:26.610 --> 00:39:29.880
- Thank you so much. - Is that what matters right now?

00:39:31.250 --> 00:39:32.820
Saving our country is what matters.

00:39:35.750 --> 00:39:38.450
A dream you dream alone is nothing but a delusion.

00:39:39.760 --> 00:39:42.690
This is going to happen. It's inevitable.

00:39:43.190 --> 00:39:45.760
All we have to do is create the pretext.

00:39:51.170 --> 00:39:52.170
Here.

00:39:53.270 --> 00:39:54.270
Here.

00:39:58.440 --> 00:39:59.940
My dear boy, Kim Tae Hyun...

00:40:00.340 --> 00:40:01.340
Yes, sir.

00:40:02.040 --> 00:40:03.350
Are the preparations proceeding without a hitch?

00:40:03.610 --> 00:40:06.320
Yes, sir. As instructed, we have twice the required personnel.

00:40:06.480 --> 00:40:07.520
Listen.

00:40:10.220 --> 00:40:12.190
You can't afford any mistakes this time.

00:40:12.960 --> 00:40:14.560
I will not fail you again.

00:40:16.390 --> 00:40:17.960
Those soldiers we're sending...

00:40:18.390 --> 00:40:21.560
Their only purpose is to train hard and die a worthy death.

00:40:22.200 --> 00:40:23.270
Yes, sir. That's correct.

00:40:23.630 --> 00:40:28.440
Those boys will be fertilizer for the boundless growth of our nation.

00:40:31.240 --> 00:40:33.310
Ensure they get a good burial plot. Somewhere with a good breeze.

00:40:34.810 --> 00:40:35.840
Yes, sir. Understood.

00:40:38.480 --> 00:40:40.380
Hey. Get me a glass of water over here.

00:40:41.150 --> 00:40:44.190
- Hey, Tae Hyun. Self-serve here. - Right.

00:40:44.350 --> 00:40:46.290
- I'll get it. - Thank you.

00:40:48.520 --> 00:40:49.829
- Darn it. - Gosh.

00:40:49.830 --> 00:40:51.290
- Darn it. Hey. - Goodness.

00:40:51.790 --> 00:40:53.160
I'm so sorry.

00:40:53.300 --> 00:40:55.100
I'll get you another cup right away. Sorry.

00:40:56.000 --> 00:40:58.370
- It's fine. Don't worry about it. - I'll get you another one.

00:40:58.730 --> 00:41:00.440
- Unity! - Unity.

00:41:00.900 --> 00:41:02.810
What are you doing, saluting a civilian?

00:41:03.510 --> 00:41:05.510
- Go on. - Take care, sir.

00:41:14.580 --> 00:41:18.220
You wouldn't take my offered hand, and now you send this surprise gift.

00:41:18.590 --> 00:41:22.760
You mean the Black Eagle Investigation Team?

00:41:24.260 --> 00:41:28.200
General Oh. We still have Black Eagles in our country.

00:41:29.030 --> 00:41:31.030
It is a wonderful surprise, isn't it?

00:41:35.640 --> 00:41:36.810
Let me ask you something.

00:41:37.970 --> 00:41:39.880
There are no Black Eagles in our country.

00:41:42.180 --> 00:41:45.010
The people you sent will soon meet the same fate.

00:41:52.660 --> 00:41:54.760
(Jo Sang Hoon, 1st sweep)

00:41:54.820 --> 00:41:57.630
(1st sweep: Yeouido 40, Press 200, Secure holding for minimum 500)

00:41:58.730 --> 00:42:01.230
Good thing they didn't notice we switched out the body cam.

00:42:02.200 --> 00:42:04.370
So, they're going to kill us, right?

00:42:04.530 --> 00:42:07.200
Yes. We're the Black Eagle Investigation Team, after all.

00:42:07.940 --> 00:42:10.770
They'll send soldiers to the MDL's northernmost point,

00:42:11.010 --> 00:42:13.040
then shell their position and kill all of them.

00:42:13.580 --> 00:42:16.550
Then they'll frame the North Korean Army for it.

00:42:17.550 --> 00:42:21.380
As a pretext, they attack the North, forcing them to retaliate.

00:42:21.650 --> 00:42:24.620
And just like that, it's war.

00:42:24.750 --> 00:42:27.390
I'm sorry, but that sounds completely insane.

00:42:27.460 --> 00:42:29.930
The idea that their goal is to start a war...

00:42:30.330 --> 00:42:32.360
and for the military to do it under civilian direction.

00:42:33.960 --> 00:42:36.900
An official notice is already out. For all of our arrests.

00:42:37.170 --> 00:42:39.070
Gosh, they don't waste any time, do they?

00:42:41.600 --> 00:42:43.870
They plan to start their operation at 10pm tonight.

00:42:44.070 --> 00:42:46.480
(November 29, 2025, at 10pm, Target sectors R-D4, XG-07)

00:42:48.980 --> 00:42:52.980
- Then it's time to start our war. - Yes.

00:43:00.590 --> 00:43:02.420
(Command center)

00:43:02.520 --> 00:43:04.290
(Special Mission Unit Rules of Conduct)

00:43:28.720 --> 00:43:30.150
Company, attention!

00:43:31.350 --> 00:43:33.419
Salute the company commander!

00:43:33.420 --> 00:43:34.790
- Unity! - Unity!

00:43:36.460 --> 00:43:37.590
Unity!

00:43:42.900 --> 00:43:43.930
As you were!

00:43:46.800 --> 00:43:50.840
Sir! For the infiltration drill, all 82 personnel are accounted for!

00:43:51.170 --> 00:43:53.280
- At ease. - At ease!

00:43:54.810 --> 00:43:56.180
At ease!

00:43:58.980 --> 00:44:01.520
Through this live combat infiltration drill,

00:44:02.080 --> 00:44:03.950
we'll prove we can counter any provocation with one fatal blow.

00:44:04.590 --> 00:44:06.820
It will prove we are more than capable of doing so.

00:44:07.420 --> 00:44:09.990
Show them what we're made of. Understood?

00:44:10.330 --> 00:44:12.090
- Yes, sir! - Yes, sir!

00:44:19.500 --> 00:44:20.940
About face!

00:44:22.770 --> 00:44:26.280
Commencing infiltration drill, effective immediately!

00:44:26.540 --> 00:44:27.680
- Move out! - Move out!

00:44:42.590 --> 00:44:44.460
Team Beta, upon arrival at sector B-24,

00:44:44.530 --> 00:44:48.130
put on the op vests stationed at the rally point and await orders.

00:44:48.460 --> 00:44:49.469
Understood?

00:44:49.470 --> 00:44:51.170
- Yes, sir! - Yes, sir!

00:44:55.770 --> 00:44:57.710
(Bird investigation)

00:45:00.710 --> 00:45:01.710
What's this?

00:45:10.790 --> 00:45:11.890
Unity!

00:45:14.860 --> 00:45:17.190
- Unity! - Unity!

00:45:17.530 --> 00:45:18.530
At ease.

00:45:23.100 --> 00:45:24.130
Unity!

00:45:25.230 --> 00:45:26.240
At ease.

00:45:28.940 --> 00:45:30.710
Transmitting fire-mission data now.

00:45:30.840 --> 00:45:35.740
Origin, 9, 8, 7, 6, 5, 4, 3, 2, 1, 0. Altitude, 150m.

00:45:35.810 --> 00:45:37.710
Sector B-24, 18 high-explosive rounds.

00:45:37.880 --> 00:45:41.220
I repeat. Sector B-24, 18 high-explosive rounds. Over.

00:45:41.650 --> 00:45:43.649
Seagull One, applying fire data.

00:45:43.650 --> 00:45:45.520
Seagull Two, applying fire data.

00:45:45.750 --> 00:45:48.060
Seagull Three, applying fire data. Over.

00:46:00.300 --> 00:46:03.010
ETA to sector B-24 is 10:30pm.

00:46:04.240 --> 00:46:07.080
All Seagull units, prepare to fire. Report when ready.

00:46:07.140 --> 00:46:08.539
Seagull One, ready to fire!

00:46:08.540 --> 00:46:10.050
Seagull Two, ready to fire!

00:46:10.110 --> 00:46:12.450
- Seagull Three, ready to fire! - We're ready, sir!

00:46:12.510 --> 00:46:13.650
Awaiting your command, sir.

00:46:37.740 --> 00:46:40.009
Put on your op vests now. Move!

00:46:40.010 --> 00:46:41.310
- Move! - Move!

00:46:51.250 --> 00:46:54.860
- Fire at 10pm sharp. - Fire at 10pm sharp.

00:46:54.920 --> 00:46:57.360
- Fire at 10pm sharp. - Order from command.

00:46:57.430 --> 00:46:59.160
Artillery, time on target 10pm. Over.

00:47:09.370 --> 00:47:11.270
- Fall in! - Fall in!

00:47:12.470 --> 00:47:15.210
This is Team Beta. All personnel are wearing op vests.

00:47:15.280 --> 00:47:16.350
Awaiting orders.

00:47:16.980 --> 00:47:18.180
This is Team Beta.

00:47:18.450 --> 00:47:21.680
All personnel have op vests on. Awaiting orders, do you copy?

00:47:21.980 --> 00:47:25.350
Fire on all of them, pigs and vests. I want them obliterated.

00:47:31.860 --> 00:47:32.960
What is this?

00:47:37.870 --> 00:47:40.770
Hey, what's that? This is crazy.

00:47:41.900 --> 00:47:43.540
What is this operation?

00:47:46.710 --> 00:47:47.710
What is this?

00:47:51.010 --> 00:47:53.120
This is Team Beta. Do you copy?

00:47:53.280 --> 00:47:55.149
This is Team Beta. Respond.

00:47:55.150 --> 00:47:57.050
- Just cut the comms. - Yes, sir.

00:47:58.490 --> 00:48:00.590
One minute to fire.

00:48:03.690 --> 00:48:05.030
It's a great strength to have you,

00:48:06.060 --> 00:48:08.100
my comrades, at my side for the new world.

00:48:09.900 --> 00:48:10.970
We have 30 seconds.

00:48:13.040 --> 00:48:14.100
Colonel Kim.

00:48:38.890 --> 00:48:39.900
What?

00:48:43.770 --> 00:48:46.130
- Did you hear that? - I didn't hear anything.

00:48:47.440 --> 00:48:48.870
I don't think I heard any artillery fire.

00:48:49.200 --> 00:48:50.610
Hey, what happened?

00:48:52.910 --> 00:48:54.580
(Warning)

00:49:02.120 --> 00:49:04.150
Are you certain you relayed the correct firing time?

00:49:05.650 --> 00:49:08.290
Why don't I hear any darn artillery fire?

00:49:08.960 --> 00:49:10.330
Because we didn't fire, sir.

00:49:11.090 --> 00:49:14.600
What did you just say? Say that again, you jerk!

00:49:14.660 --> 00:49:17.100
I'm sorry, sir, but we cannot follow that order.

00:49:17.670 --> 00:49:19.430
You scum, do you have a death wish?

00:49:19.840 --> 00:49:22.340
We cannot fire on civilians, sir.

00:49:22.370 --> 00:49:25.210
(Warning)

00:49:33.320 --> 00:49:34.420
Civilians?

00:49:34.720 --> 00:49:36.150
All artillery units are pulling out.

00:49:46.530 --> 00:49:49.199
Captain, a civilian vehicle is approaching.

00:49:49.200 --> 00:49:50.270
What are you talking about?

00:49:50.900 --> 00:49:53.700
- What's going on? - Captain.

00:49:53.940 --> 00:49:56.200
- Stay sharp. On alert. - Hey, stay sharp! On alert!

00:49:56.270 --> 00:49:59.640
- Yes, sir! On alert! - Hey, get them!

00:49:59.670 --> 00:50:00.680
On alert!

00:50:03.910 --> 00:50:05.950
- There's a box truck coming down. - What on earth?

00:50:06.010 --> 00:50:07.550
- Hey! Muzzles up! - It's coming down!

00:50:07.880 --> 00:50:09.580
- I think it's a bus! - It looks full of civilians.

00:50:09.650 --> 00:50:11.350
Stay calm and don't cross your lines of fire!

00:50:15.690 --> 00:50:17.229
Sergeant, it looks like a civilian vehicle.

00:50:17.230 --> 00:50:18.330
There are civilians inside.

00:50:26.000 --> 00:50:27.799
- Stop! - Stop! Sergeant!

00:50:27.800 --> 00:50:29.469
- Stop! - What's the situation?

00:50:29.470 --> 00:50:31.270
- A bus has come in. - Hold your position.

00:50:34.480 --> 00:50:36.810
We'll hold our position and wait for orders.

00:50:39.950 --> 00:50:43.020
Hey! Give me remote access now. I'll do it myself.

00:50:43.350 --> 00:50:46.320
They're saying there are civilians in Sector B24.

00:50:46.890 --> 00:50:50.030
Hey, who cares if they're civilians or soldiers?

00:50:50.090 --> 00:50:52.290
We'll just say the North Korean Army killed them all anyway.

00:50:53.130 --> 00:50:54.200
Darn it.

00:50:54.560 --> 00:50:55.800
What are you doing?

00:50:56.000 --> 00:50:57.500
Give me remote access!

00:51:02.940 --> 00:51:04.070
What are you doing?

00:51:05.140 --> 00:51:06.170
Inside that sector,

00:51:06.880 --> 00:51:08.840
there are civilians.

00:51:10.750 --> 00:51:14.620
Hey, you got a death wish? Patch me through now!

00:51:15.020 --> 00:51:17.050
Give me remote access now!

00:51:20.720 --> 00:51:22.520
- Connect him. - Connecting now, sir.

00:51:26.700 --> 00:51:27.730
Connection established.

00:51:28.000 --> 00:51:29.459
- What was that? - There's a one-star here.

00:51:29.460 --> 00:51:30.530
This is insane.

00:51:30.730 --> 00:51:32.370
- We're all going to die, aren't we? - Something's definitely wrong.

00:51:33.900 --> 00:51:34.900
Goodness.

00:51:53.320 --> 00:51:54.360
Now,

00:51:55.360 --> 00:51:56.830
the great undertaking begins.

00:52:35.200 --> 00:52:37.100
- Let's go! - Hurry up!

00:52:40.540 --> 00:52:42.870
- Looks like it's starting. - Right. I'd better get my shots.

00:52:43.170 --> 00:52:44.970
- Okay, camera on. Get in there. - Right.

00:52:45.040 --> 00:52:46.040
Go.

00:52:51.180 --> 00:52:52.310
(Elements Guerrilla Concert, With our comrades-in-arms)

00:52:58.350 --> 00:52:59.390
What is this?

00:53:00.890 --> 00:53:03.490
Here you go, Elements light sticks.

00:53:08.500 --> 00:53:09.999
Here you go.

00:53:10.000 --> 00:53:12.270
Elements light sticks for you too.

00:53:12.330 --> 00:53:15.470
(Elements Guerrilla Concert, With our comrades-in-arms)

00:53:24.610 --> 00:53:26.950
Here, take two. There you go.

00:53:28.580 --> 00:53:29.750
- Thank you. - Here.

00:53:32.320 --> 00:53:34.519
Attack!

00:53:34.520 --> 00:53:36.990
I said open fire, darn it!

00:53:37.090 --> 00:53:40.630
What are you waiting for, you jerks? I said, open fire!

00:53:40.800 --> 00:53:42.160
You scums.

00:53:42.300 --> 00:53:44.330
(32S 7808)

00:53:50.340 --> 00:53:51.340
Welcome.

00:53:59.280 --> 00:54:00.780
- Hello. - Hello.

00:54:00.850 --> 00:54:02.750
- Elements, bringing you happiness. - Elements, bringing you happiness.

00:54:03.020 --> 00:54:04.420
- We are Elements! - We are Elements!

00:54:04.490 --> 00:54:06.720
(Elements Guerrilla Concert, With our comrades-in-arms)

00:54:06.790 --> 00:54:08.490
What are you doing, you jerks?

00:54:09.220 --> 00:54:10.790
They say they can't obey the order, sir.

00:54:11.230 --> 00:54:12.460
Hey, Tae Hyun.

00:54:12.690 --> 00:54:13.900
Tae Hyun!

00:54:15.400 --> 00:54:17.370
What are you doing, you jerks?

00:54:17.730 --> 00:54:20.540
Hey, stupid idiot. Get out!

00:54:34.950 --> 00:54:37.220
(Elements Guerrilla Concert, With our comrades-in-arms)

00:54:50.800 --> 00:54:51.830
So pretty.

00:54:52.370 --> 00:54:55.170
Okay, Elements, it's time to go.

00:54:55.240 --> 00:54:56.670
(Elements Guerrilla Concert, With our comrades-in-arms)

00:55:07.920 --> 00:55:09.980
Die!

00:55:16.860 --> 00:55:17.930
Shots fired!

00:55:43.590 --> 00:55:45.350
That's a reassuring sight.

00:55:45.650 --> 00:55:47.260
Those guys must have realized it by now.

00:55:47.860 --> 00:55:49.660
That what they were chasing wasn't a dream...

00:55:50.020 --> 00:55:51.330
but a delusion.

00:55:53.160 --> 00:55:55.630
They're the ones who saved us.

00:56:24.530 --> 00:56:28.530
(Elements Guerrilla Concert, With our comrades-in-arms)

00:56:29.160 --> 00:56:30.970
- Captain Kim. - Yes, sir.

00:56:33.370 --> 00:56:36.910
That Black Eagle ecological survey must have been quite the ordeal.

00:56:39.070 --> 00:56:40.980
- You've been through a lot. - Thank you, sir.

00:56:42.510 --> 00:56:43.610
It's good to see you all.

00:56:44.280 --> 00:56:45.980
- Unity. - Sir.

00:56:46.080 --> 00:56:47.120
Unity.

00:56:49.220 --> 00:56:50.850
Master Sergeant Park Jae Won...

00:56:51.150 --> 00:56:54.890
went to a lot of trouble to swap all the bombs for fireworks.

00:56:57.090 --> 00:56:58.330
But you know...

00:56:58.660 --> 00:57:01.060
Do you really need that many fireworks?

00:57:03.630 --> 00:57:05.570
I wasn't sure how many they'd need to set off.

00:57:17.550 --> 00:57:20.320
Gosh, that's a lot of fireworks.

00:57:25.520 --> 00:57:27.320
(Elements Guerrilla Concert, With our comrades-in-arms)

00:57:33.230 --> 00:57:34.230
All right, then.

00:57:35.130 --> 00:57:36.900
Shall we go take care of business?

00:57:37.870 --> 00:57:40.370
Let's go get those jerks before they all run off.

00:57:43.500 --> 00:57:44.540
We'll be on our way, sir.

00:57:44.910 --> 00:57:45.910
Unity!

00:57:46.340 --> 00:57:47.340
Unity.

00:58:09.330 --> 00:58:11.200
That jerk!

00:58:11.600 --> 00:58:13.570
I told you we should've bailed before this got messy.

00:58:13.670 --> 00:58:16.040
But won't accepting that note cause problems for us later?

00:58:16.100 --> 00:58:17.340
Just say you never got it.

00:58:17.610 --> 00:58:19.910
The CCTV at the burger joint could have caught us.

00:58:19.970 --> 00:58:21.640
Then say it was folded so you didn't see what it was.

00:58:21.740 --> 00:58:23.780
I put it straight into my pocket, so I didn't see it.

00:58:24.380 --> 00:58:25.680
I'll drive.

00:58:37.260 --> 00:58:39.190
All right, Generals!

00:58:44.070 --> 00:58:45.430
You're all under arrest.

00:58:46.600 --> 00:58:47.700
Take them all in!

00:58:48.340 --> 00:58:50.570
- What are you talking about? - What unit are you with?

00:58:50.640 --> 00:58:51.710
- Hey, freeze! - Hey!

00:58:51.770 --> 00:58:53.740
- Come with me. - Get off me, you jerk!

00:58:54.480 --> 00:58:55.580
Move it.

00:59:05.820 --> 00:59:06.820
Let go.

00:59:18.700 --> 00:59:20.170
(Deluxe Taxi)

00:59:37.950 --> 00:59:39.090
Those jerks.

00:59:42.590 --> 00:59:44.090
(Deluxe Taxi)

00:59:46.530 --> 00:59:47.860
Chief Choi, stop the car!

01:00:02.280 --> 01:00:03.610
(Deluxe Taxi)

01:00:07.980 --> 01:00:09.920
(Deluxe Taxi)

01:00:16.860 --> 01:00:18.490
(Deluxe Taxi)

01:00:34.980 --> 01:00:36.680
Chief Choi! Chief Park!

01:00:37.580 --> 01:00:38.580
Go Eun!

01:00:39.910 --> 01:00:42.080
Hey, can you get up? Can you stand?

01:00:44.990 --> 01:00:46.720
Gyeong Gu, are you okay?

01:00:47.290 --> 01:00:49.419
- What about you? You okay? - Is everyone okay?

01:00:49.420 --> 01:00:50.630
- Yes, I'm fine. - This way.

01:00:50.860 --> 01:00:52.690
- Chief Choi... - Yes?

01:01:05.370 --> 01:01:07.540
You jerks!

01:01:08.810 --> 01:01:12.150
Hey! Why?

01:01:14.650 --> 01:01:15.650
Hey!

01:01:16.420 --> 01:01:18.050
You worthless scums.

01:01:21.220 --> 01:01:24.459
- Die! - Go Eun!

01:01:24.460 --> 01:01:25.460
- Go Eun! - Go Eun!

01:01:25.461 --> 01:01:26.559
- Go Eun! - Go Eun!

01:01:26.560 --> 01:01:28.030
- You... - Go Eun!

01:01:28.330 --> 01:01:29.930
Do you have any idea what you've ruined?

01:01:32.700 --> 01:01:34.470
This was an operation...

01:01:36.170 --> 01:01:39.110
to save the country from a crisis! Darn it.

01:01:40.140 --> 01:01:42.010
A man who claims he'll save the country...

01:01:42.240 --> 01:01:44.580
treats the people who live in it worse than insects...

01:01:44.880 --> 01:01:46.780
in reality.

01:01:47.080 --> 01:01:49.850
- Isn't that the bigger problem? - Hey, you think that matters?

01:01:50.520 --> 01:01:52.150
What's the big deal about that?

01:01:53.990 --> 01:01:55.090
You people...

01:01:55.860 --> 01:01:57.260
are destined to lose.

01:02:00.430 --> 01:02:01.600
- Driver Kim! - Driver Kim!

01:02:01.660 --> 01:02:02.730
- Driver Kim! - Driver Kim!

01:02:03.000 --> 01:02:04.100
- Driver Kim! - Do Gi!

01:02:04.900 --> 01:02:06.030
Damn it.

01:02:06.930 --> 01:02:08.370
We won't know how this ends...

01:02:09.540 --> 01:02:11.170
until we get to the end.

01:02:12.140 --> 01:02:15.240
When the desperation and courage of everyone come together,

01:02:16.880 --> 01:02:18.180
it's a force to be reckoned with.

01:02:23.750 --> 01:02:24.750
Gosh.

01:02:31.690 --> 01:02:33.260
Take one more step...

01:02:34.230 --> 01:02:35.900
and see just how this ends.

01:02:36.730 --> 01:02:37.800
Do you want to see?

01:02:40.270 --> 01:02:41.570
- Do Gi! - Driver Kim!

01:02:41.640 --> 01:02:43.070
Driver Kim!

01:02:54.320 --> 01:02:55.350
Give up!

01:03:01.420 --> 01:03:02.490
You should have...

01:03:04.230 --> 01:03:06.590
just kept your head down where you belong.

01:03:07.400 --> 01:03:08.400
Why?

01:03:08.900 --> 01:03:13.730
Why on earth did you all crawl in here to die?

01:03:13.940 --> 01:03:14.940
Why?

01:03:17.270 --> 01:03:18.270
- Driver Kim! - Do Gi!

01:03:19.110 --> 01:03:21.010
- Make one move. - Driver Kim!

01:03:21.080 --> 01:03:23.440
- I'll kill him! - Driver Kim!

01:03:23.510 --> 01:03:24.510
Don't!

01:03:26.010 --> 01:03:27.380
We will never...

01:03:32.590 --> 01:03:34.160
lose to people like you.

01:03:48.940 --> 01:03:51.940
- Driver Kim! - Driver Kim!

01:03:52.010 --> 01:03:53.710
- Do Gi! - No!

01:04:24.070 --> 01:04:27.480
(To save one life is to save the world.)

01:04:27.540 --> 01:04:30.610
You have a big appetite, Chief Choi. Why aren't you eating?

01:04:30.680 --> 01:04:34.180
- I'm full. - Already? And you, Chief Park?

01:04:34.420 --> 01:04:36.250
Who taught you to grab the drumstick first?

01:04:36.320 --> 01:04:38.490
- I raised this chicken myself. - Thank you.

01:04:38.950 --> 01:04:40.450
This guy's something else.

01:04:41.890 --> 01:04:43.660
- Let's have a drink. - Okay.

01:04:44.290 --> 01:04:46.190
- Cheers. - Cheers.

01:04:54.470 --> 01:04:55.770
By the way,

01:04:56.700 --> 01:04:58.140
has this thought ever crossed your mind?

01:04:58.470 --> 01:05:00.110
- What? - What thought?

01:05:01.580 --> 01:05:04.880
If everything that happened to us never happened,

01:05:05.380 --> 01:05:06.850
what do you think our lives would be like?

01:05:08.080 --> 01:05:09.450
Do you think we ever would have met?

01:05:14.320 --> 01:05:15.990
I doubt we would have met.

01:05:16.790 --> 01:05:18.830
We'd all probably be working hard at our separate jobs.

01:05:18.890 --> 01:05:21.200
That's true. We're all dedicated to our work.

01:05:21.460 --> 01:05:23.030
You never know.

01:05:24.030 --> 01:05:27.740
When, where, or how we might have crossed paths.

01:05:29.300 --> 01:05:30.470
That's right.

01:05:31.340 --> 01:05:35.240
We could've gone on a trip one day and happened to run into each other.

01:05:38.010 --> 01:05:39.650
- Okay, I'm taking it now. - Okay.

01:05:39.680 --> 01:05:40.850
Dad, scoot in a little closer.

01:05:41.180 --> 01:05:43.880
Okay, big smiles now. One, two, three.

01:05:44.550 --> 01:05:46.020
One, two, three.

01:05:46.890 --> 01:05:48.020
Okay.

01:05:48.390 --> 01:05:50.860
It came out great. Should we get a picture of the three of us?

01:05:51.260 --> 01:05:52.330
Oh, dear.

01:05:52.830 --> 01:05:54.460
Excuse me.

01:05:55.000 --> 01:05:57.130
Excuse me, would you like me to take a picture for you?

01:05:58.730 --> 01:06:01.270
Thank you so much. That would be great.

01:06:06.210 --> 01:06:07.579
- Smile. - Okay.

01:06:07.580 --> 01:06:09.140
One, two, three.

01:06:11.110 --> 01:06:12.380
I'm so sorry.

01:06:12.450 --> 01:06:16.150
Or what if we went to a restaurant from TV and ran into one another?

01:06:16.220 --> 01:06:17.850
You're not late. We were just getting started.

01:06:17.920 --> 01:06:20.090
- You guys started eating? - This place is seriously good.

01:06:20.150 --> 01:06:21.190
I can't wait to see your wedding dress.

01:06:21.260 --> 01:06:22.260
- I come here sometimes. - Oh, really?

01:06:22.320 --> 01:06:23.560
- You know that one? - It's good, right?

01:06:23.620 --> 01:06:24.630
- Yes, it's really good. - Right?

01:06:25.030 --> 01:06:26.930
- Have some meat. - No, you go ahead.

01:06:26.990 --> 01:06:28.260
- Oh, gosh. - What is it?

01:06:28.330 --> 01:06:30.330
This place is amazing. I've been here before.

01:06:32.870 --> 01:06:36.370
Or we could've just bumped into each other walking down the street.

01:06:44.010 --> 01:06:45.050
Are you okay?

01:06:45.550 --> 01:06:48.020
Yes. Thank you.

01:06:48.320 --> 01:06:49.680
- No problem. - All right.

01:06:50.850 --> 01:06:51.850
Thank you.

01:06:53.220 --> 01:06:54.790
- Right. - Right.

01:07:15.740 --> 01:07:17.040
When you think about it,

01:07:17.310 --> 01:07:18.750
I guess we would've met again, no matter what.

01:07:20.380 --> 01:07:22.980
Somehow, I feel like we were bound to meet.

01:07:23.020 --> 01:07:25.350
I guess it was meant to be.

01:07:26.290 --> 01:07:28.060
- Here, have a drink. - Thanks.

01:07:33.690 --> 01:07:34.760
Me too.

01:07:49.310 --> 01:07:51.579
- All right, how about a toast? - Yes!

01:07:51.580 --> 01:07:52.780
Cheers.

01:08:09.100 --> 01:08:10.160
Go Eun.

01:08:11.000 --> 01:08:11.970
Yes?

01:08:12.600 --> 01:08:13.830
Could you take care of the bill?

01:08:14.970 --> 01:08:16.040
Sure.

01:08:22.080 --> 01:08:24.950
You look exhausted. Trouble sleeping again last night?

01:08:25.210 --> 01:08:28.150
No. I think I'm coming down with a cold.

01:08:28.180 --> 01:08:30.250
When that happens, it's better to just get some proper rest.

01:08:31.520 --> 01:08:32.850
I'm fine.

01:08:33.350 --> 01:08:34.760
I actually feel better when I'm working.

01:08:36.790 --> 01:08:38.230
You sure don't look like it.

01:09:12.860 --> 01:09:15.860
(Rainbow Transport)

01:09:21.370 --> 01:09:25.170
You get a steady paycheck, so you better earn it.

01:09:25.840 --> 01:09:28.110
Is killing one little wench that hard?

01:09:29.010 --> 01:09:32.910
Finding an agency that kills people is harder than you'd think.

01:09:33.950 --> 01:09:37.280
Turn on the TV. Hitmen are a dime a dozen.

01:09:42.360 --> 01:09:43.390
You're just...

01:09:44.090 --> 01:09:48.330
making excuses for your own incompetence.

01:09:49.860 --> 01:09:53.830
I'm sorry, ma'am. I'll try looking a little harder.

01:09:56.570 --> 01:09:59.910
About your missing sister, Rim Bok Ja...

01:10:00.140 --> 01:10:02.740
Someone says she was seen overseas. I think we'll find her soon.

01:10:02.810 --> 01:10:03.810
Hey!

01:10:05.110 --> 01:10:08.980
What's this "sister" nonsense? I've never even laid eyes on her.

01:10:10.550 --> 01:10:14.660
Instead of her appearing suddenly demanding half the inheritance,

01:10:16.020 --> 01:10:20.830
getting rid of her quietly overseas is a lot cleaner, isn't it?

01:10:28.370 --> 01:10:30.170
I believe I've found a contractor.

01:10:31.740 --> 01:10:33.440
The meeting spot...

01:10:34.340 --> 01:10:35.910
Didn't you say it was by the port?

01:10:36.540 --> 01:10:39.710
So why are we driving further up into the mountains?

01:10:42.250 --> 01:10:45.620
I think there might be an error with the GPS.

01:10:45.690 --> 01:10:47.720
- Rerouting. - That's strange.

01:10:47.890 --> 01:10:51.790
We're probably losing service because you drove us out to nowhere!

01:11:06.270 --> 01:11:09.940
There's a taxi right here. I'll go see if it's in service.

01:11:13.280 --> 01:11:15.120
(Deluxe Taxi)

01:11:19.250 --> 01:11:20.720
Is this a pottery studio?

01:11:31.800 --> 01:11:32.900
Pottery...

01:11:33.800 --> 01:11:34.870
An axe?

01:11:36.300 --> 01:11:37.770
Excuse me.

01:11:41.940 --> 01:11:43.180
Pardon me.

01:11:45.910 --> 01:11:48.450
I'm a little lost.

01:11:49.320 --> 01:11:52.020
Is this taxi in service?

01:12:08.000 --> 01:12:10.040
His leg...

01:12:12.940 --> 01:12:15.710
I just saw the taxi here, so...

01:12:21.480 --> 01:12:23.680
- Need a ride? - No.

01:12:24.490 --> 01:12:26.620
I don't want a ride.

01:12:29.120 --> 01:12:30.860
You saw something you shouldn't have.

01:12:33.260 --> 01:12:34.700
Something you shouldn't have seen.

01:12:35.560 --> 01:12:36.860
Gosh.

01:12:39.730 --> 01:12:42.270
What? Isn't this a pottery kiln?

01:12:44.840 --> 01:12:45.910
Wait a minute.

01:12:46.910 --> 01:12:47.910
I know...

01:12:48.280 --> 01:12:50.080
this is going to sound incredibly strange,

01:12:50.510 --> 01:12:52.610
but I've actually been desperately...

01:12:53.880 --> 01:12:55.380
looking for someone just like you.

01:12:56.920 --> 01:12:58.120
What's taking her so long?

01:12:58.990 --> 01:13:00.020
Hey!

01:13:20.870 --> 01:13:21.910
Haven't we...

01:13:22.510 --> 01:13:23.540
met somewhere...

01:13:24.380 --> 01:13:25.950
before?

01:13:47.430 --> 01:13:48.770
If you have time,

01:13:49.240 --> 01:13:52.870
would you like to have a glass of wine with me?

01:13:54.610 --> 01:13:56.040
